<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12347" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dătĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		do, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the act of giving, allotting, distributing; giving up,
				surrender</i> (good prose, but rare).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in datione,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 3, 9 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: legum ( = latio), * <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr.
				2, 22, 60</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signi dationem Palamedes invenit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					7, 56, 57, § 202</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legati, opp. ademptio legati,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					34, 4, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">partis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					45, 1, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The right to give</i> or <i>convey
				away</i> property: <i>right of alienation</i>,
			* <i><span class="en">Liv. 39, 19</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A gift</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">datio Dei permanet pistis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg. Sirach. 11, 17</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
